 <flight_control name="FCS: myrocket">

  <property value="6.27">fcs/rail-travel-ft</property>
  <channel name="Rail">
   <fcs_function name="fcs/rail-margin-ft">
     <function>
       <difference>
         <difference>
           <property>position/h-agl-ft</property>
           <property>ic/h-agl-ft</property>
         </difference>
         <product>
           <property>fcs/rail-travel-ft</property>
           <sin><property>attitude/theta-rad</property></sin>
         </product>
       </difference>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>
   <switch name="fcs/off-rail">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="OR" value="1.0">
       fcs/rail-margin-ft gt 0.0
       simulation/sim-time-sec gt 2.0
     </test>
   </switch>
  </channel>

  <property value="10000.0">fcs/target-apogee-ft</property>

  <property value="0.2">fcs/sep-delay-sec</property>
  <property value="0.0">fcs/coast-sec</property>
  <property value="0.0">fcs/gate-alt-ft</property>
  <property value="20.0">fcs/tilt-max-deg</property>
  <property value="1.0">fcs/use-inhibits</property>
  <property value="1.0">fcs/k-cd</property>
  <property value="1.0">fcs/k-stack</property>
  <property value="1.0">fcs/k-cn</property>
  <property value="0.0">fcs/tipoff-pitch-ftlb</property>
  <property value="0.0">fcs/tipoff-yaw-ftlb</property>
  <property value="9.0">fcs/stage1-weight-lbs</property>

  <channel name="Airbrakes">

   <fcs_function name="fcs/coast-vt2">
     <description>Terminal-velocity squared for the coast, ft2/s2.
       vt2 = 2*W / (rho * S * Cd), built from live weight and density so the
       estimate adapts to mass and altitude without being told about them.

       Cd IS THE STOWED VALUE ON PURPOSE. The estimate therefore answers
       "where do I go if I stow the brake now", and the loop's job is to drive
       that quantity to the target: the moment it reaches the target, stowing
       the brake delivers the target, which is exactly when braking should
       stop.

       A version including the current brake position in Cd was tried and is
       much worse: nominal-day error went from +28 ft to +383 ft and peak
       deployment fell from 1.00 to 0.38. The mechanism is that proportional
       control needs a standing error to hold the brake out at all, since the
       command is kp times the error. With the brake in the estimate that
       standing error is a real apogee error, so the loop reads its own
       deployment as the problem being solved and retracts early. With the
       stowed form the standing error is measured against a prediction that is
       deliberately higher than the truth, and costs nothing.

       0.45 is the nominal stowed figure and is deliberately not adjusted to
       the true drag of the as-built airframe, which a flight computer would
       not know.</description>
     <function>
       <quotient>
         <product>
           <value> 2.0 </value>
           <property>inertia/weight-lbs</property>
         </product>
         <product>
           <property>atmosphere/rho-slugs_ft3</property>
           <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
           <value> 0.45 </value>
         </product>
       </quotient>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>

   <fcs_function name="fcs/coast-x">
     <description>v^2 / vt2, the argument of the log term.</description>
     <function>
       <quotient>
         <product>
           <property>velocities/h-dot-fps</property>
           <property>velocities/h-dot-fps</property>
         </product>
         <property>fcs/coast-vt2</property>
       </quotient>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>

   <fcs_function name="fcs/coast-ln">
     <description>ln(1+x) as a lookup rather than a natural-log operator, so
       the file does not depend on which maths elements a given JSBSim build
       exposes.</description>
     <function>
       <table>
         <independentVar lookup="row">fcs/coast-x</independentVar>
         <tableData>
                0.000    0.0000
                0.050    0.0488
                0.100    0.0953
                0.150    0.1398
                0.200    0.1823
                0.300    0.2624
                0.400    0.3365
                0.500    0.4055
                0.600    0.4700
                0.700    0.5306
                0.800    0.5878
                0.900    0.6419
                1.000    0.6931
                1.250    0.8109
                1.500    0.9163
                2.000    1.0986
                2.500    1.2528
                3.000    1.3863
                4.000    1.6094
                6.000    1.9459
         </tableData>
       </table>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>

   <fcs_function name="fcs/apogee-estimate-ft">
     <description>Closed-form apogee for a ballistic coast against quadratic
       drag at constant density:

           h_apogee = h + (vt2 / 2g) * ln(1 + v^2 / vt2)

       This replaces an energy estimate h + k*v^2/2g with a fixed k. A fixed
       factor cannot work: the share of kinetic energy lost to drag is not
       constant along the coast. With k = 0.75 the estimate runs about 535 ft
       high at burnout and about 615 ft low in mid-coast, changing sign in
       between. Mean absolute error over the coast falls from 314 ft to 20 ft
       with the form below.

       That error profile mattered because control authority is not spread
       evenly: holding the brake fully out for the first 4 s of coast gives
       most of the total authority (crosscheck.py authority gives the
       numbers). The estimator therefore has to be right early,
       which is exactly where the fixed-factor form was worst.

       Under +/-10% drag, +/-5% thrust and +/-5% mass, closed-loop apogee
       spread falls from 364 ft to 66 ft and worst-case error from 412 ft to
       35 ft. Open loop is 1480 ft.</description>
     <function>
       <sum>
         <property>position/h-agl-ft</property>
         <product>
           <quotient>
             <property>fcs/coast-vt2</property>
             <value> 64.348 </value>
           </quotient>
           <property>fcs/coast-ln</property>
         </product>
       </sum>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>

   <fcs_function name="fcs/apogee-error-ft">
     <function>
       <difference>
         <property>fcs/apogee-estimate-ft</property>
         <property>fcs/target-apogee-ft</property>
       </difference>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>

   <pure_gain name="fcs/brake-cmd-raw">

     <input>fcs/apogee-error-ft</input>
     <gain> 0.001 </gain>
     <clipto>
       <min> 0.0 </min>
       <max> 1.0 </max>
     </clipto>
   </pure_gain>

   <switch name="fcs/brake-cmd-gated">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="AND" value="fcs/brake-cmd-raw">
       propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs lt 1.0
       propulsion/engine[1]/thrust-lbs lt 1.0
       velocities/h-dot-fps gt 0.0
       position/h-agl-ft gt 1500.0
     </test>
   </switch>

   <kinematic name="fcs/airbrake-actuator">
     <input>fcs/brake-cmd-gated</input>
     <traverse>
       <setting>
         <position> 0.0 </position>
         <time>     0.0 </time>
       </setting>
       <setting>
         <position> 1.0 </position>
         <time>     0.5 </time>
       </setting>
     </traverse>
     <output>fcs/airbrake-pos-norm</output>
   </kinematic>

  </channel>

  <channel name="Staging">

   <switch name="fcs/burnout-det">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="OR" value="1.0">
       fcs/burnout-det ge 0.5
       <test logic="AND">
         simulation/sim-time-sec gt 1.0
         propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs lt 1.0
       </test>
     </test>
   </switch>
   <switch name="fcs/t-burnout">
     <default value="fcs/t-burnout"/>
     <test logic="AND" value="simulation/sim-time-sec">
       fcs/burnout-det lt 0.5
     </test>
   </switch>
   <fcs_function name="fcs/t-since-bo">
     <function>
       <product>
         <property>fcs/burnout-det</property>
         <difference>
           <property>simulation/sim-time-sec</property>
           <property>fcs/t-burnout</property>
         </difference>
       </product>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>
   <fcs_function name="fcs/t-ign-decision">
     <function>
       <sum>
         <property>fcs/sep-delay-sec</property>
         <property>fcs/coast-sec</property>
       </sum>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>
   <switch name="fcs/staged">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="AND" value="1.0">
       fcs/burnout-det ge 0.5
       fcs/t-since-bo ge fcs/sep-delay-sec
     </test>
   </switch>
   <fcs_function name="fcs/tilt-deg">
     <function>
       <difference>
         <value>90.0</value>
         <property>attitude/theta-deg</property>
       </difference>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>
   <!-- Record this FCS frame before the decision latch changes. -->
   <switch name="fcs/lit-tilt-deg">
     <default value="fcs/lit-tilt-deg"/>
     <test logic="AND" value="fcs/tilt-deg">
       fcs/decision-now lt 0.5
     </test>
   </switch>
   <switch name="fcs/lit-alt-ft">
     <default value="fcs/lit-alt-ft"/>
     <test logic="AND" value="position/h-agl-ft">
       fcs/decision-now lt 0.5
     </test>
   </switch>
   <switch name="fcs/decision-now">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="AND" value="1.0">
       fcs/staged ge 0.5
       fcs/t-since-bo ge fcs/t-ign-decision
     </test>
   </switch>
   <switch name="fcs/gates-ok">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="OR" value="1.0">
       fcs/use-inhibits lt 0.5
       <test logic="AND">
         position/h-agl-ft ge fcs/gate-alt-ft
         fcs/tilt-deg le fcs/tilt-max-deg
       </test>
     </test>
   </switch>
   <switch name="fcs/sust-lit">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="OR" value="1.0">
       fcs/sust-lit ge 0.5
       <test logic="AND">
         fcs/decision-now ge 0.5
         fcs/gates-ok ge 0.5
         fcs/lockout lt 0.5
       </test>
     </test>
   </switch>
   <switch name="fcs/lockout">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="OR" value="1.0">
       fcs/lockout ge 0.5
       <test logic="AND">
         fcs/decision-now ge 0.5
         fcs/gates-ok lt 0.5
         fcs/sust-lit lt 0.5
       </test>
     </test>
   </switch>
   <switch name="fcs/stage1-weight-cmd">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="AND" value="fcs/stage1-weight-lbs">
       fcs/staged lt 0.5
     </test>
     <output>inertia/pointmass-weight-lbs[1]</output>
   </switch>
   <switch name="fcs/sustainer-ignite-cmd">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="AND" value="1.0">
       fcs/sust-lit gt 0.5
     </test>
     <output>propulsion/engine[1]/set-running</output>
   </switch>
   <switch name="fcs/sustainer-throttle-cmd">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="AND" value="1.0">
       fcs/sust-lit gt 0.5
     </test>
     <output>fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[1]</output>
   </switch>
   <switch name="fcs/tipoff-on">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="AND" value="1.0">
       fcs/staged ge 0.5
       fcs/t-since-bo lt fcs/tipoff-end
     </test>
   </switch>
   <fcs_function name="fcs/tipoff-end">
     <function>
       <sum>
         <property>fcs/sep-delay-sec</property>
         <value>0.05</value>
       </sum>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>
  </channel>

 </flight_control>

 <aerodynamics>

  <axis name="DRAG">

    <function name="aero/force/Drag_mach">
       <description>Axial drag coefficient vs Mach number</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/k-cd</property>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <table>
            <independentVar lookup="row">velocities/mach</independentVar>
            <tableData>
              0.00   0.45
              0.50   0.45
              0.80   0.48
              0.95   0.72
              1.05   0.78
              1.30   0.70
              2.00   0.58
              3.00   0.48
            </tableData>
          </table>
       </product>
    </function>

    <function name="aero/force/Drag_airbrake">
       <description>Air-brake drag increment. dCd = 2.0 at full deployment,
       referenced to body cross-section. Control authority (apogee lost if
       held fully deployed through the coast): crosscheck.py authority.</description>
       <product>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <property>fcs/airbrake-pos-norm</property>
          <value> 2.0 </value>
       </product>
    </function>

    <function name="aero/force/Drag_crossflow">
       <description>Crossflow drag (alpha), c = 52.00: c sin^2|sin| (v6).</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/off-rail</property>
          <difference><value>1.0</value><property>fcs/staged</property></difference>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <product>
            <value> 52.0046351981478 </value>
            <sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin>
            <abs><sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin></abs>
            <sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin>
          </product>
       </product>
    </function>

    <function name="aero/force/Drag_beta">
       <description>Crossflow drag (beta), c = 52.00: c sin^2|sin| (v6).</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/off-rail</property>
          <difference><value>1.0</value><property>fcs/staged</property></difference>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <product><value>52.0046351981478</value><abs><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></abs><abs><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></abs><abs><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></abs></product>
       </product>
    </function>

      <function name="aero/force/Drag_crossflow_sust">
       <description>Crossflow drag (alpha), c = 25.29: c sin^2|sin| (v6).</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/off-rail</property>
          <property>fcs/staged</property>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <product>
            <value> 25.2937498613835 </value>
            <sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin>
            <abs><sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin></abs>
            <sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin>
          </product>
       </product>
    </function>
    <function name="aero/force/Drag_beta_sust">
       <description>Crossflow drag (beta), c = 25.29: c sin^2|sin| (v6).</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/off-rail</property>
          <property>fcs/staged</property>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <product><value>25.2937498613835</value><abs><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></abs><abs><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></abs><abs><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></abs></product>
       </product>
    </function>
      <function name="aero/force/Drag_stack_extra">
       <description>Stack friction-drag increment before separation (v6): booster body and fin
       wetted area, turbulent Cf = 0.00233; dCD = 0.247 on the body cross-section,
       scaled by fcs/k-stack for sensitivity.</description>
       <product>
          <difference><value>1.0</value><property>fcs/staged</property></difference>
          <property>fcs/k-stack</property>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <value> 0.2467 </value>
       </product>
    </function>
  </axis>

  <axis name="LIFT">

    <function name="aero/force/Lift_alpha">
       <description>Stack normal force (before separation), Barrowman.</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/k-cn</property>
          <property>fcs/off-rail</property>
          <difference><value>1.0</value><property>fcs/staged</property></difference>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
